  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1023 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nThe UA pattern over the SW CONUS remains largely unchanged through \nthe weekend. The 500 mb high near the Four Corners amplifies to \nnearly 600 dam by Thursday while keeping us under a zonal extension \nof its parent ridge. As such, PoPs later this week may be in \njeopardy as this ridge axis remains parked keeping the brunt of \nprecip chances well to our north. Friday evening holds the most \npotential for our panhandle counties to see slight PoPs provided a \nshortwave trough rotates far enough SW around the ridge securing \nbrief height falls/increased ascent. Thereafter, the mid-level high \ncrawls our way and deamplifies slightly before shifting atop the \nregion early next week. High temps are unlikely to waver too much in \nthis pattern with upper 90s on the Caprock and sub-105 readings \nelsewhere.",
